# Veil — line-ending policy.
#
# Normalize ALL text files to LF in the repo and on checkout, regardless of a
# contributor's platform or core.autocrlf setting. Without this, editing on
# Windows/WSL rewrites every file's line endings and turns each diff into
# repo-wide CRLF churn. `text=auto` lets git detect binary files automatically.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF-only so `bash` (including WSL bash invoked from
# Windows) does not choke on carriage returns in constructs like
# `set -euo pipefail\r`. (Redundant with the rule above, but explicit.)
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf

# PowerShell is happy with either, but keep it consistent with the repo's
# default so diffs stay clean.
*.ps1        text eol=lf

# Binary-ish files git should never touch.
*.png        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.gif        binary
*.ico        binary
*.pdf        binary
